/**
 * covers.js — real cover images, as data.
 *
 * Generated by the scripts in tools/, not hand-written. Regenerate with:
 *
 *     .\tools\fetch-covers.ps1     query Open Library
 *     .\tools\fix-covers.ps1       retry poor matches, verify each URL
 *     .\tools\final-covers.ps1     strict author audit — the one that decides
 *
 * Every id below survived three checks:
 *
 *   1. the matched edition had to be credited to one of the book's
 *      authors, so a right-looking title by the wrong writer never gets
 *      through. This is what caught "Almond" by Allen Say, a book called
 *      "The Kama Sutra of Business" standing in for Business Sutra, a
 *      different "The Evolution of Everything", and two Nancy Drew
 *      titles credited to the Hardy Boys ghostwriter;
 *   2. foreign-language editions were accepted only on an exact title
 *      match, which is how the Japanese printings of Norwegian Wood and
 *      Before the Coffee Gets Cold kept their real covers;
 *   3. the image URL had to actually return a JPEG.
 *
 * Books flagged `needsReview` in the catalogue are never looked up at
 * all. We do not know which book they are, so we do not go looking for a
 * picture of one. A guessed cover is a lie with a picture on it.
 *
 * COVERS ARE METADATA, NOT MARKUP. Nothing here is referenced by a
 * component directly: seed-books.js attaches the URL to the book record,
 * and one function — resolveCover() in cover-policy.js — decides what any
 * book actually shows. Phase 2 can point these at cloud storage without a
 * single view changing.
 */

